Cities and Countries #title

$image lesson4-map.jpg

London is a city.
Paris is a city too.
New York is a city.
Tokyo is also a city.

London is in England.
Paris is in France.
New York is in the United States.
Tokyo is in Japan.

England, France, the United States, and Japan are countries.

Which city is in England?
* [London. #ok]
* [Paris. #fail]
* [Tokyo. #fail]
-

London is in England.

Which city is in France?
* [Paris. #ok]
* [London. #fail]
* [New York. #fail]
-

Paris is in France.

Paris is a big city.
Tokyo is bigger than Paris.
Tokyo is the biggest of the four cities.

$image lesson4-cities.jpg

There are many houses in a big city.
There are many people in London.
There are even more people in Tokyo.

A town is smaller than a city.
There are fewer people in a town.

Is Tokyo bigger than Paris?
* [Yes, it is. #ok]
* [No, Paris is bigger. #fail]
-

Tokyo is bigger than Paris.

Are there many people in a big city?
* [Yes, there are. #ok]
* [No, there are not. #fail]
-

There are many people in a big city.

The people in England are the English.
The people in France are the French.
The people in the United States are the Americans.
The people in Japan are the Japanese.

Who are the English?
* [The people in England. #ok]
* [The people in France. #fail]
* [The people in Japan. #fail]
-

The English are the people in England.

Dialogue #title

@man Where do you live?
@helen We live in London.
@man And what country is London in?
@john London is in England.
